# These files are build recipes consumed by make, cmake and sh on Linux.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, and the root
# .gitattributes pins `Makefile` and `*.sh` to LF -- but not `Makefile.<variant>`
# and not `CMakeLists.txt`, both of which are used here. Without this file the
# six rpath variants would be checked out with CRLF, and make would put a
# carriage return INSIDE the rpath string it bakes into the product:
# `$ORIGIN/../lib\r` resolves to nothing, and every recipe line would have a
# stray \r appended to the command.
#
# That failure would not appear in the tree that created the corpus, where the
# files are already LF. It would appear on a fresh clone. A fixture that works
# only where it was written is the exact failure this directory exists to catch,
# so the rule is stated here rather than left to the root file's patterns.
Makefile.*     eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt eol=lf
